  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "A goalless round-of-16 tie at the Maracanã approaching the half hour. Uruguay, without the suspended Luis Suárez, kept a compact shape, and Colombia went long to get around it."
    },
    {
      "label": "Build-up",
      "text": "A long ball dropped towards the edge of the Uruguay box, where Aguilar won the header and nodded it back into the path of James, arriving in the space in front of the defence."
    },
    {
      "label": "The technique",
      "text": "With back to goal, James cushioned the ball on the chest, swivelled in the same movement and struck a left-footed volley before it landed. The chest touch set the ball up rather than killing it, so no defender had time to close."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "From outside the box the dipping volley flew beyond Muslera's reach, came down off the underside of the crossbar and over the line. Striking early gave the keeper no time to set."
    }
  ],
  "note": "From memory of the footage: Aguilar's knock-down and James's chest-and-volley in off the bar are accurate; build-up, positions and kits are approximate. Commentary is original."
}
